{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RVgkBHLDTXSahjcrBvQ8Z9","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Aurora Awareness Revamp â€” Handoff for researchPrime â†’ Crucible\n2\t\n3\t**Written:** 2026-06-11, end of the dashboard-build session (context getting long).\n4\t**Author:** Claude (Opus 4.8), from John's live feedback after using the new dashboard.\n5\t**Purpose:** carry John's thinking + grounded facts into a FRESH Claude Code session\n6\tthat runs **researchPrime** (to gather outside ideas) and then **Crucible** (to re-plan\n7\tthe Aurora dashboard AND the backend collection/curation). Do NOT start building from\n8\tthis doc â€” it is the brief for research + planning.\n9\t\n10\t---\n11\t\n12\t## 0. The one-paragraph version\n13\t\n14\tThe dashboard shipped and looks great, but using it exposed that Aurora is optimizing\n15\tfor the wrong thing at the surface, and possibly at collection too. John doesn't want an\n16\tops console or a taxonomy sunburst â€” he wants an **agentic-AI awareness instrument**: a\n17\thuman-readable, decision-oriented view of *what's newly worth knowing in agentic AI*\n18\t(systems, theories, harnesses, **models + pricing + best-in-class**, benchmarks, skills,\n19\ttools, templates), **why it matters**, and **whether to adopt it** â€” plus an honest\n20\tanswer to \"is this pipeline earning its ~$1/night?\" The data is partly already there\n21\t(352 priced models collected, never surfaced); the surfaces and the collection targets\n22\tneed rethinking. Research the best ways to do this, then Crucible a revision.\n23\t\n24\t---\n25\t\n26\t## 1. The (re-sharpened) North Star\n27\t\n28\tFrom John, verbatim intent (2026-06-11): Aurora exists to **make John aware of all current\n29\tadvances in agentic AI** â€” agentic systems, theories, approaches, advances in **harnesses**,\n30\tthe **models** that feed them, the **benchmarks**, and new **skills / templates / tools**.\n31\tThis serves THREE jobs, co-equal:\n32\t\n33\t1. **Educate John** â€” keep him current on the field.\n34\t2. **Guide generation of new agents** â€” inform what he builds (GWL agents, etc.).\n35\t3. **Feed the agentic systems** â€” make all of it available to the GWL agentic system, to\n36\t   Claude (via the **Helping Hand** skill), and to Gemini (via Helping Hand) for retrieval.\n37\t\n38\tThis sharpens the existing locked revamp North Star (`docs/AURORA_REVAMP_PLAN.md`,\n39\t2026-06-06: \"felt, trustworthy value AND robust architecture, co-equal\"). THIS handoff is\n40\tabout the **felt-value / awareness half**, now concrete from real dashboard use.\n41\t\n42\t> Drift guard for the planner: every proposed surface or collection change must serve\n43\t> awareness + adoption-decision + agent-feeding. A prettier ops console or a richer\n44\t> taxonomy that does not make John *more aware and better-decided* is bloat.\n45\t\n46\t---\n47\t\n48\t## 2. What John said after using the dashboard (distilled, faithful)\n49\t\n50\t| # | Reaction | The real ask |\n51\t|---|---|---|\n52\t| A | **Morning report:** fine. | Keep it. |\n53\t| B | \"Nothing new last night but we still spent money.\" Saw a \"deep think skill\" found (looks like a researchPrime / Gemini Deep-Think analog). | **Honest value accounting:** what did the spend buy? Is it finding things worth the money? (see Â§3 facts) |\n54\t| C | **Suggested adoption** â€” is this something I act on? | Make adoption **actionable**: a tab to review candidate adoptions, each with a **human-readable summary, risks, advantages, why adopt / why not**, and an accept/decline. |\n55\t| D | **Health page: \"completely not helpfulâ€¦ looks like something a computer might read.\"** | **Human-readable health + value:** plain-English \"is it working, is it worth it, what's wrong, what should I think about.\" Not JSON-shaped signals. |\n56\t| E | **What was new:** mildly interesting, but wants it **by category** â€” skills, tools, templates, agents, AND **models (open-source + proprietary LLMs), most-recent / current best-in-class, with pricing**. And: \"am I actually collecting anything?\" | A **category intelligence** surface: per-category \"what's the current best-in-class + what's newly notable,\" not a raw nightly dump. Surface the models+pricing that's already collected. |\n57\t| F | **Catalog map: not interested.** Wants a **knowledge / relationship map** â€” \"what's out there and how it relates,\" emergent reasonable classifications. Recalls prior notes/ideas (garbled in transcription as \"Pinochet map / Lorentz map\" â€” likely a named viz type: concept map / knowledge graph / landscape / constellation / Sankey / Voronoi / force-directed). | A **human-readable relationship map** of the agentic-AI landscape â€” how systems / harnesses / models / skills relate â€” that helps him *understand the space*, not just browse a taxonomy. Research the best technique. |\n58\t| G | Meta: have **Fable 5** (or a deep-think pass) do a hard, honest \"is this genuinely useful to a human like me?\" critique. Consider a separate **critical-analysis tool** (later session). | Bake an **honest-critic deliverable** into the research/plan: does Aurora earn its keep, and what would make it genuinely valuable? |\n59\t\n60\t---\n61\t\n62\t## 3. Grounded facts (read-only, live KB + reports, 2026-06-11) â€” use these, don't re-derive blind\n63\t\n64\t**Collection is real but skewed to papers.** New artifacts, last 7 days (first_seen):\n65\tpapers dominate (â‰ˆ15â€“21/day), tools trickle, **skills/agents/templates are rare**, models 1â€“2/day.\n66\tLast night (06â€‘11): **8 papers, 0 skills/tools/agents** â†’ that's why \"nothing new\" showed\n67\t(the morning panel's finds-new excludes papers/models). ~20 candidates were screened+rejected.\n68\t**So the $/night largely buys arxiv-paper harvesting + screening, not the harnesses/models/skills\n69\tJohn cares about.** This is the central value question: *are we pointed at the right sources?*\n70\t\n71\t**The models goldmine is collected but unsurfaced.** `models` table = **352 rows, ALL priced**\n72\t(`price_in_usd_per_mtok`, `price_out_usd_per_mtok`, `context_in_tokens`, `max_output_tokens`,\n73\t`modalities`, `tool_use`, `reasoning_mode`, `knowledge_cutoff`, `license_class`, `released_at`,\n74\t`deprecation_date`, provider/family/version). The dashboard shows none of this. BUT data quality\n75\tis mixed: junk rows exist (e.g. `openrouter/pareto-code` price `-1000000` sentinel; `owl/alpha` $0)\n76\tâ†’ a \"current best-in-class models + pricing\" surface needs **ranking + junk filtering + a\n77\t'best-in-class' notion**, which don't exist yet.\n78\t\n79\t**Benchmarks are NOT collected.** `model_benchmarks` = **0 rows**. John explicitly wants \"the\n80\tbenches.\" This is a collection gap, not just a surface gap.\n81\t\n82\t**Taste/usage loop exists but is thin.** `interest_score` (taste) is live on ~30 finds + heuristic\n83\tfallback; `hh_events` usage is mostly `surfaced` with near-zero `loaded` (adoption 24%, n=21, all-time).\n84\tSuggested-adoption is currently a passive metric, not an actionable workflow (matches reaction C).\n85\t\n86\t**Key existing pieces to reuse, not rebuild:** the read-only dashboard package (`dashboard/`,\n87\tblueprint-mountable), `kb/aurora.db` schema (artifacts / models / embeddings.domain_path /\n88\tlink_health / hh_events / costs / runs), `reports/`, Helping Hand MCP (`helping-hand-plugin/`),\n89\t`docs/INTEREST_PROFILE.md` (John's taste profile), the taste scorer (`roles/taste.py`).\n90\t\n91\t---\n92\t\n93\t## 4. The gap, stated plainly (the thing to fix)\n94\t\n95\tAurora today is a **discovery+hygiene pipeline with an ops dashboard**. John wants an\n96\t**agentic-AI awareness+decision instrument**. The deltas:\n97\t\n98\t1. **Surface: ops â†’ awareness.** Replace machine-readable health with plain-English\n99\t   \"is it working / worth it / what to think about.\" Replace the nightly dump with\n100\t   per-category \"current best-in-class + newly notable, with why-it-matters.\"\n101\t2. **Surface: passive â†’ actionable adoption.** A review queue: candidate â†’ human summary,\n102\t   risks, advantages, recommendation, accept/decline â†’ feeds Helping Hand.\n103\t3. **Surface: taxonomy â†’ knowledge/relationship map.** A human-readable map of how the\n104\t   landscape relates (research the technique).\n105\t4. **Collection: re-target.** Less arxiv-paper volume; more harnesses, best-in-class\n106\t   models (+pricing, already half-there), benchmarks (currently zero), high-signal skills/\n107\t   tools/templates. Add a \"best-in-class / current frontier\" notion + ranking + junk filtering.\n108\t5. **Honesty: value accounting.** A real answer to \"what did the spend buy, and is it worth it.\"\n109\t\n110\t---\n111\t\n112\t## 5. Research questions for researchPrime (the EXECUTION brief)\n113\t\n114\tStakes: medium-high (informs a real revision + ongoing spend). Validate claims; resist\n115\tbandwagon; prefer OBSERVED/CORROBORATED evidence; return full + executive + agent-impl summaries.\n116\t\n117\t1. **Awareness surfaces for fast-moving fields.** How do the best \"stay-current\" products /\n118\t   newsletters / dashboards / radars (e.g. tech radars, model-comparison sites, leaderboards,\n119\t   \"state of AI\" reports) surface a fast-moving technical field to a smart non-specialist for\n120\t   BOTH education AND decision-making? What patterns make them genuinely used vs ignored?\n121\t2. **Best-in-class model intelligence.** What's the best way to present a living \"current\n122\t   best-in-class LLMs (open + proprietary), with pricing, context, modalities, reasoning,\n123\t   benchmarks\" view? What sources/benchmarks are authoritative and machine-collectable for an\n124\t   automated nightly pipeline? (We already collect 352 priced models; benchmarks = 0.)\n125\t3. **Adoption-decision UX.** Best patterns for a human \"should I adopt this?\" review queue\n126\t   for tools/skills/agents â€” what info (risks, advantages, fit, effort, provenance) and what\n127\t   interaction make the decision fast and trustworthy.\n128\t4. **Knowledge / relationship maps.** Survey techniques for a human-readable map of \"what's\n129\t   out there and how it relates\" in a technical landscape â€” concept maps, knowledge graphs,\n130\t   landscape/quadrant maps, force-directed networks, Sankey/flow, Voronoi/treemap, embedding\n131\t   projections (UMAP/t-SNE), \"constellation\" maps. Which best convey relationships + emergent\n132\t   classification for ~hundreds of items, and are buildable dependency-light + offline? Recommend.\n133\t5. **Collection targeting.** For \"advances in agentic AI\" (systems, theories, harnesses,\n134\t   models, benchmarks, skills/tools/templates), what are the highest-signal sources and\n135\t   ranking strategies â€” so the nightly spend buys frontier-relevant items, not arxiv volume?\n136\t6. **Honest value framing.** How should a personal intelligence pipeline measure and report\n137\t   its own ROI/value to its owner, honestly (avoiding vanity metrics)?\n138\t\n139\t**Required deliverable beyond the survey:** a blunt, Fable-5-style critique â€” *given the North\n140\tStar (Â§1) and the facts (Â§3), is Aurora currently worth running, and what 3â€“5 changes would\n141\tmake it genuinely valuable to a human like John?* No flattery.\n142\t\n143\t---\n144\t\n145\t## 6. Then: Crucible\n146\t\n147\tFeed researchPrime's output + this handoff into **Crucible** (greenfield-on-existing-data,\n148\tbrownfield-aware) to forge a Foreman-ready plan for: (a) the dashboard revision (awareness +\n149\tadoption + human health + knowledge map), and (b) the backend collection/curation revision\n150\t(re-targeting, best-in-class models+benchmarks, ranking). Keep the read-only dashboard\n151\tpackage + KB schema; evolve, don't rebuild (per the AuroraTwo verdict). Lock the Â§1 North Star\n152\tat Stage 0; surface the Â§4 deltas as the scope; let Crucible's Shark-Tank pressure-test it.\n153\t\n154\t## 7. Pointers\n155\t- This session's build: `docs/foreman-handoff-dashboard/` (DESCRIPTION / IMPLEMENTATION-PLAN /\n156\t  EXECUTION-LOG / DASHBOARD.md) + `dashboard/` package + `aurora_dashboard.py`.\n157\t- Prior revamp: `docs/AURORA_REVAMP_PLAN.md` (North Star 2026-06-06). AuroraTwo verdict:\n158\t  `docs/AURORA_AURORATWO_RESEARCH.md` (evolve, don't rebuild; \"knowledge maps\" is a named\n159\t  Aurora concept).\n160\t- Plan + schema: `docs/NIGHTLY_SWEEP_PLAN.md`, `kb/schema.sql`. Taste: `docs/INTEREST_PROFILE.md`,\n161\t  `roles/taste.py`. Serving: `helping-hand-plugin/`.\n162\t- Session playbook + constraints: `C:\\dev\\aurora\\CLAUDE.md` (read-only against KB; never read\n163\t  `.env`; real schedules 01:07â€“06:47; working tree is production).\n164\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2f64445c-2549-447b-b8ef-967bae126936","uuid":"56b34d7f-fa4c-471f-94e0-7801ebfb2df7","timestamp":"2026-06-12T00:32:33.784Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\dev\\aurora\\docs\\aurora-awareness-revamp\\HANDOFF.md","content":"# Aurora Awareness Revamp â€” Handoff for researchPrime â†’ Crucible\n\n**Written:** 2026-06-11, end of the dashboard-build session (context getting long).\n**Author:** Claude (Opus 4.8), from John's live feedback after using the new dashboard.\n**Purpose:** carry John's thinking + grounded facts into a FRESH Claude Code session\nthat runs **researchPrime** (to gather outside ideas) and then **Crucible** (to re-plan\nthe Aurora dashboard AND the backend collection/curation). Do NOT start building from\nthis doc â€” it is the brief for research + planning.\n\n---\n\n## 0. The one-paragraph version\n\nThe dashboard shipped and looks great, but using it exposed that Aurora is optimizing\nfor the wrong thing at the surface, and possibly at collection too. John doesn't want an\nops console or a taxonomy sunburst â€” he wants an **agentic-AI awareness instrument**: a\nhuman-readable, decision-oriented view of *what's newly worth knowing in agentic AI*\n(systems, theories, harnesses, **models + pricing + best-in-class**, benchmarks, skills,\ntools, templates), **why it matters**, and **whether to adopt it** â€” plus an honest\nanswer to \"is this pipeline earning its ~$1/night?\" The data is partly already there\n(352 priced models collected, never surfaced); the surfaces and the collection targets\nneed rethinking. Research the best ways to do this, then Crucible a revision.\n\n---\n\n## 1. The (re-sharpened) North Star\n\nFrom John, verbatim intent (2026-06-11): Aurora exists to **make John aware of all current\nadvances in agentic AI** â€” agentic systems, theories, approaches, advances in **harnesses**,\nthe **models** that feed them, the **benchmarks**, and new **skills / templates / tools**.\nThis serves THREE jobs, co-equal:\n\n1. **Educate John** â€” keep him current on the field.\n2. **Guide generation of new agents** â€” inform what he builds (GWL agents, etc.).\n3. **Feed the agentic systems** â€” make all of it available to the GWL agentic system, to\n   Claude (via the **Helping Hand** skill), and to Gemini (via Helping Hand) for retrieval.\n\nThis sharpens the existing locked revamp North Star (`docs/AURORA_REVAMP_PLAN.md`,\n2026-06-06: \"felt, trustworthy value AND robust architecture, co-equal\"). THIS handoff is\nabout the **felt-value / awareness half**, now concrete from real dashboard use.\n\n> Drift guard for the planner: every proposed surface or collection change must serve\n> awareness + adoption-decision + agent-feeding. A prettier ops console or a richer\n> taxonomy that does not make John *more aware and better-decided* is bloat.\n\n---\n\n## 2. What John said after using the dashboard (distilled, faithful)\n\n| # | Reaction | The real ask |\n|---|---|---|\n| A | **Morning report:** fine. | Keep it. |\n| B | \"Nothing new last night but we still spent money.\" Saw a \"deep think skill\" found (looks like a researchPrime / Gemini Deep-Think analog). | **Honest value accounting:** what did the spend buy? Is it finding things worth the money? (see Â§3 facts) |\n| C | **Suggested adoption** â€” is this something I act on? | Make adoption **actionable**: a tab to review candidate adoptions, each with a **human-readable summary, risks, advantages, why adopt / why not**, and an accept/decline. |\n| D | **Health page: \"completely not helpfulâ€¦ looks like something a computer might read.\"** | **Human-readable health + value:** plain-English \"is it working, is it worth it, what's wrong, what should I think about.\" Not JSON-shaped signals. |\n| E | **What was new:** mildly interesting, but wants it **by category** â€” skills, tools, templates, agents, AND **models (open-source + proprietary LLMs), most-recent / current best-in-class, with pricing**. And: \"am I actually collecting anything?\" | A **category intelligence** surface: per-category \"what's the current best-in-class + what's newly notable,\" not a raw nightly dump. Surface the models+pricing that's already collected. |\n| F | **Catalog map: not interested.** Wants a **knowledge / relationship map** â€” \"what's out there and how it relates,\" emergent reasonable classifications. Recalls prior notes/ideas (garbled in transcription as \"Pinochet map / Lorentz map\" â€” likely a named viz type: concept map / knowledge graph / landscape / constellation / Sankey / Voronoi / force-directed). | A **human-readable relationship map** of the agentic-AI landscape â€” how systems / harnesses / models / skills relate â€” that helps him *understand the space*, not just browse a taxonomy. Research the best technique. |\n| G | Meta: have **Fable 5** (or a deep-think pass) do a hard, honest \"is this genuinely useful to a human like me?\" critique. Consider a separate **critical-analysis tool** (later session). | Bake an **honest-critic deliverable** into the research/plan: does Aurora earn its keep, and what would make it genuinely valuable? |\n\n---\n\n## 3. Grounded facts (read-only, live KB + reports, 2026-06-11) â€” use these, don't re-derive blind\n\n**Collection is real but skewed to papers.** New artifacts, last 7 days (first_seen):\npapers dominate (â‰ˆ15â€“21/day), tools trickle, **skills/agents/templates are rare**, models 1â€“2/day.\nLast night (06â€‘11): **8 papers, 0 skills/tools/agents** â†’ that's why \"nothing new\" showed\n(the morning panel's finds-new excludes papers/models). ~20 candidates were screened+rejected.\n**So the $/night largely buys arxiv-paper harvesting + screening, not the harnesses/models/skills\nJohn cares about.** This is the central value question: *are we pointed at the right sources?*\n\n**The models goldmine is collected but unsurfaced.** `models` table = **352 rows, ALL priced**\n(`price_in_usd_per_mtok`, `price_out_usd_per_mtok`, `context_in_tokens`, `max_output_tokens`,\n`modalities`, `tool_use`, `reasoning_mode`, `knowledge_cutoff`, `license_class`, `released_at`,\n`deprecation_date`, provider/family/version). The dashboard shows none of this. BUT data quality\nis mixed: junk rows exist (e.g. `openrouter/pareto-code` price `-1000000` sentinel; `owl/alpha` $0)\nâ†’ a \"current best-in-class models + pricing\" surface needs **ranking + junk filtering + a\n'best-in-class' notion**, which don't exist yet.\n\n**Benchmarks are NOT collected.** `model_benchmarks` = **0 rows**. John explicitly wants \"the\nbenches.\" This is a collection gap, not just a surface gap.\n\n**Taste/usage loop exists but is thin.** `interest_score` (taste) is live on ~30 finds + heuristic\nfallback; `hh_events` usage is mostly `surfaced` with near-zero `loaded` (adoption 24%, n=21, all-time).\nSuggested-adoption is currently a passive metric, not an actionable workflow (matches reaction C).\n\n**Key existing pieces to reuse, not rebuild:** the read-only dashboard package (`dashboard/`,\nblueprint-mountable), `kb/aurora.db` schema (artifacts / models / embeddings.domain_path /\nlink_health / hh_events / costs / runs), `reports/`, Helping Hand MCP (`helping-hand-plugin/`),\n`docs/INTEREST_PROFILE.md` (John's taste profile), the taste scorer (`roles/taste.py`).\n\n---\n\n## 4. The gap, stated plainly (the thing to fix)\n\nAurora today is a **discovery+hygiene pipeline with an ops dashboard**. John wants an\n**agentic-AI awareness+decision instrument**. The deltas:\n\n1. **Surface: ops â†’ awareness.** Replace machine-readable health with plain-English\n   \"is it working / worth it / what to think about.\" Replace the nightly dump with\n   per-category \"current best-in-class + newly notable, with why-it-matters.\"\n2. **Surface: passive â†’ actionable adoption.** A review queue: candidate â†’ human summary,\n   risks, advantages, recommendation, accept/decline â†’ feeds Helping Hand.\n3. **Surface: taxonomy â†’ knowledge/relationship map.** A human-readable map of how the\n   landscape relates (research the technique).\n4. **Collection: re-target.** Less arxiv-paper volume; more harnesses, best-in-class\n   models (+pricing, already half-there), benchmarks (currently zero), high-signal skills/\n   tools/templates. Add a \"best-in-class / current frontier\" notion + ranking + junk filtering.\n5. **Honesty: value accounting.** A real answer to \"what did the spend buy, and is it worth it.\"\n\n---\n\n## 5. Research questions for researchPrime (the EXECUTION brief)\n\nStakes: medium-high (informs a real revision + ongoing spend). Validate claims; resist\nbandwagon; prefer OBSERVED/CORROBORATED evidence; return full + executive + agent-impl summaries.\n\n1. **Awareness surfaces for fast-moving fields.** How do the best \"stay-current\" products /\n   newsletters / dashboards / radars (e.g. tech radars, model-comparison sites, leaderboards,\n   \"state of AI\" reports) surface a fast-moving technical field to a smart non-specialist for\n   BOTH education AND decision-making? What patterns make them genuinely used vs ignored?\n2. **Best-in-class model intelligence.** What's the best way to present a living \"current\n   best-in-class LLMs (open + proprietary), with pricing, context, modalities, reasoning,\n   benchmarks\" view? What sources/benchmarks are authoritative and machine-collectable for an\n   automated nightly pipeline? (We already collect 352 priced models; benchmarks = 0.)\n3. **Adoption-decision UX.** Best patterns for a human \"should I adopt this?\" review queue\n   for tools/skills/agents â€” what info (risks, advantages, fit, effort, provenance) and what\n   interaction make the decision fast and trustworthy.\n4. **Knowledge / relationship maps.** Survey techniques for a human-readable map of \"what's\n   out there and how it relates\" in a technical landscape â€” concept maps, knowledge graphs,\n   landscape/quadrant maps, force-directed networks, Sankey/flow, Voronoi/treemap, embedding\n   projections (UMAP/t-SNE), \"constellation\" maps. Which best convey relationships + emergent\n   classification for ~hundreds of items, and are buildable dependency-light + offline? Recommend.\n5. **Collection targeting.** For \"advances in agentic AI\" (systems, theories, harnesses,\n   models, benchmarks, skills/tools/templates), what are the highest-signal sources and\n   ranking strategies â€” so the nightly spend buys frontier-relevant items, not arxiv volume?\n6. **Honest value framing.** How should a personal intelligence pipeline measure and report\n   its own ROI/value to its owner, honestly (avoiding vanity metrics)?\n\n**Required deliverable beyond the survey:** a blunt, Fable-5-style critique â€” *given the North\nStar (Â§1) and the facts (Â§3), is Aurora currently worth running, and what 3â€“5 changes would\nmake it genuinely valuable to a human like John?* No flattery.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Then: Crucible\n\nFeed researchPrime's output + this handoff into **Crucible** (greenfield-on-existing-data,\nbrownfield-aware) to forge a Foreman-ready plan for: (a) the dashboard revision (awareness +\nadoption + human health + knowledge map), and (b) the backend collection/curation revision\n(re-targeting, best-in-class models+benchmarks, ranking). Keep the read-only dashboard\npackage + KB schema; evolve, don't rebuild (per the AuroraTwo verdict). Lock the Â§1 North Star\nat Stage 0; surface the Â§4 deltas as the scope; let Crucible's Shark-Tank pressure-test it.\n\n## 7. Pointers\n- This session's build: `docs/foreman-handoff-dashboard/` (DESCRIPTION / IMPLEMENTATION-PLAN /\n  EXECUTION-LOG / DASHBOARD.md) + `dashboard/` package + `aurora_dashboard.py`.\n- Prior revamp: `docs/AURORA_REVAMP_PLAN.md` (North Star 2026-06-06). AuroraTwo verdict:\n  `docs/AURORA_AURORATWO_RESEARCH.md` (evolve, don't rebuild; \"knowledge maps\" is a named\n  Aurora concept).\n- Plan + schema: `docs/NIGHTLY_SWEEP_PLAN.md`, `kb/schema.sql`. Taste: `docs/INTEREST_PROFILE.md`,\n  `roles/taste.py`. Serving: `helping-hand-plugin/`.\n- Session playbook + constraints: `C:\\dev\\aurora\\CLAUDE.md` (read-only against KB; never read\n  `.env`; real schedules 01:07â€“06:47; working tree is production).\n","numLines":164,"startLine":1,"totalLines":164}}}
